PM Norvik today confirmed Veridia's commitment to maintaining defence spending at 2.7% of GDP during a parliamentary address 💰. The budget focuses on naval upgrades and strengthening cybersecurity infrastructure to address emerging regional security concerns. Opposition leaders have voiced worries about the impact on other public services. No vote has been scheduled yet 🗳️.
#Veridia #DefenceBudget
@VeridiaNewsBriefs

Prime Minister Aleksander Norvik was in Silverwood today, attending the state funeral for the late President Elara Vance 🕊️. He conveyed Veridia’s condolences to Vance’s family and the people of Norland, signing the official condolence book. The delegation's presence highlights the strong diplomatic relationship between Veridia and Norland 🤝. A sombre occasion for regional leaders.
#Norland #Veridia
@VeridianDispatch

Ministers met in Luxembourg today to finalize a new migration deal with North African countries 🤝. The agreement focuses on border management improvements and faster asylum processing to curb Mediterranean arrivals. Financial support and cooperation against human trafficking are key components of the accord. Details on funding and repatriation are still being worked out 💰.
#Migration #EUAfrica
@GlobalNewsBriefs

EU ministers met today in Luxembourg to finalize a new agreement with North African countries. The deal aims to improve border management and speed up asylum processing to curb Mediterranean crossings 🌊. It includes increased financial support and collaboration to combat human trafficking, though specifics are still being worked out. More details to follow as negotiations conclude! 🤝
#Migration #EUAfrica
